d 'RESHAPEHELPER': module to diagnose the dataset and suggest (never run) the likely reshape command
d
d  A dry-run advisor for Stata's hardest data-management command.
d reshapehelper never reshapes your data. It scans variable names
d for wide patterns (numeric suffixes, string suffixes, @ mid-name
d stubs, doubly-wide double indices), finds candidate i and j
d variables (honoring xtset/tsset and svyset declarations), decides
d the likely direction, composes the reshape command, and TESTS it
d on a small sample inside preserve/restore, iterating on reshape's
d own errors (string j, spaces in j, duplicates within i-j,
d non-constant variables) until the suggestion runs or the blocker
d is diagnosed. Output: an ASCII before/after diagram of what the
d suggestion would do, the suggested syntax with its dry-run
d verdict (also stored in r(cmd) and $reshapehelper_cmd, written
d unwrapped to a viewable SMCL file, and offered as a click-to-run
d link), or - when it cannot discern the design - a numbered
d checklist of what to fix or specify before running reshapehelper
d again. Flags transpose jobs that are really xpose/sxpose
d problems. 
d
d KW: reshape; data management; long; wide
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.0
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Texas 2036
d Support: email eric.a.booth@@gmail.com
d
f ../e/example_reshapehelper.do
f reshapehelper.ado
f reshapehelper.sthlp
